00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:03,040
B2.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:15,425
Daniel has found another talk by an environmental expert about how to protect wetlands, listen with him and complete the notes below.

3
00:00:15,425 --> 00:00:19,940
Wetlands are really important for wildlife.

4
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:23,750
We should try our best to protect wetlands.

5
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:27,580
There are two main problems for wetlands today.

6
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:32,510
First, people use the land for farms and buildings.

7
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:35,870
Another problem is caused by tourists.

8
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:43,050
As people move through wetlands, they may bring trouble to the animals there or harm the plants.

9
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:52,180
To help solve these problems, governments can take action by making laws to stop people from building on wetlands.

10
00:00:52,180 --> 00:01:02,940
Governments can also make laws to reduce the number of tourists visiting wetlands and make sure visitors do no harm while they are there.

11
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:08,770
Local communities should also work together to help protect wetlands.

12
00:01:08,770 --> 00:01:15,470
To keep the ecosystem healthy, they can help clean up pollution and guide tourists.

13
00:01:15,470 --> 00:01:21,530
They can also plant trees to attract more birds, animals and insects.
